step2_extraction.content:
You will be given clinical notes and a series of yes/no questions. For each question, answer with 1 (yes) or 0 (no) if it is not.

Questions:
{prompt_questions}

Clinical notes:
{sentence}

Provide your answers in the following JSON format:
{
  "reasoning": "Brief explanation of your answers",
  "extractions": [
    {"question": 0, "reasoning": "why yes/no", "answer": 1},
    {"question": 1, "reasoning": "why yes/no", "answer": 0},
    {"question": 2, "reasoning": "why yes/no", "answer": 1}
  ]
}

Answer all questions. Use 1 for yes, 0 for no. Output valid JSON only.

step3_initialization.content:
We are fitting a concept bottleneck model (CBM) to predict whether or not a patient has the flu from their clinical notes. The goal is to identify interpretable yes/no concepts that clinicians can use to predict probability of having the flu.

A meta-concept must be a yes/no question like "Does the note mention the patient having...?".

Given data analysis, these are the top phrases associated with flu:
{top_features_df}

YOUR TASK:
Propose {max_meta_concepts} candidate meta-concepts for the CBM.

Propose candidates in JSON format:
{
  "reasoning": "Step-by-step explanation",
  "concepts": [
    {
      "concept": "Does the note mention the patient having nausea?",
      "is_risk_factor": true,
      "words": ["nausea", "vomiting"]
    },
    ...
  ]
}

